                <pb facs="0402" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/117a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-15T23:00:00-04:00">September 15,
                            1942—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>229. Colonel McBride is leaving shortly for Liberia as a special representative
                    of the President. Please render him all possible assistance in the performance
                    of his mission. Colonel Upston of the Office of the Chief of Staff will be with
                    him, and it is hoped that he may also be accommodated at the Legation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
